        topic: "Mixed",
        fp: "Defendant was playing in a high-stakes backroom poker game. An argument erupted between Defendant and a fellow gambler over a $10,000 pot. The gambler stood up, pulled an 8-inch hunting knife from his boot, and lunged across the table, slashing Defendant across the forearm. The gambler shouted, 'I will slit your throat!' Defendant leaped backward, drew a licensed semi-automatic pistol from his waistband, and pointed it at the gambler's chest. Seeing the aimed firearm, the gambler instantly dropped his knife onto the carpet, raised both hands high in the air with open palms, stepped backward six feet against the wall, and screamed: 'I quit, don't shoot, I drop the knife!' Defendant stood staring at the gambler for three seconds, leveled his pistol directly at the gambler's forehead, shouted 'Nobody cuts me and walks away!', and pulled the trigger. The bullet struck the gambler between the eyes, killing him instantly. The jurisdiction defines murder and manslaughter at common law.",
