        fp: "An engineering company entered into a written contract with an oil refinery operator to overhaul an industrial catalytic cracking unit for $100,000, payable upon completion on June 1. On May 15, after the contractor had completed 50% of the overhaul and incurred $30,000 in labor and parts, a dispute arose regarding technical welding standards. The contractor claimed that the refinery's welding specs were ambiguous, while the refinery claimed the contractor's work was defective. To resolve the bona fide dispute, the parties executed a signed written agreement on May 20: 'Refinery agrees to pay Contractor $60,000 on June 1, and Contractor agrees to accept said $60,000 in full and complete satisfaction and discharge of all claims arising under the original May contract, upon payment thereof.' On June 1, the refinery refused to pay the $60,000 or any other amount. The contractor immediately brought an action against the refinery seeking $100,000 under the original contract.",
